{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7JkhNtA5JGF8Gw8w3zZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Before I draft, a few questions. Each answer would change what the pitch says.\n\n1. **What's different from last time, and why do you think the first campaign fell short?** Many backers will remember getting refunded, so the pitch needs to deal with that directly. I can already point to a lower target, the bank's pledge, the $1 lease and the 46 volunteers. Is there anything else, like a new board, a clearer plan, or a cheaper approach to the roof?\n\n2. **How will the cinema pay its way once it's open?** People will want to know it won't close again in two years. Do you have rough running costs, ticket prices, or a break-even figure (e.g. \"we need X tickets a week; we used to sell 180\")?\n\n3. **What are the mechanics?** I assume the deadline is June 30, 2027, and that the crowd needs to raise $60,000 to unlock the bank's $25,000. Is that right? Is the campaign all-or-nothing again, with refunds if you miss? And are there reward tiers I should mention?\n\n4. **What are the names?** I need the cinema's name, the town's name and the bank's name, if the bank is happy to be named.\n\n5. **Is there one story or detail that sums up what the cinema meant to the town?** For example, a long-running Saturday matinee, a first date that became a marriage, or what people do now instead of making the 38-mile drive.\n\nIf you don't know some of these, say so and I'll write without them rather than guess."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":245,"cache_read_input_tokens":9519,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":245},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent