{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7Jn1RNuZXNZnxYDFh3W","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<final_document>\n**Bring Back the Majestic**\n\nThe Majestic on Main Street closed in 2022. Since then, seeing a film on a big screen has meant a 76-mile round trip, because the nearest cinema is 38 miles away.\n\nWe're a group of volunteers working to reopen it. We need $85,000 to replace the projector and sound system and to fix the roof.\n\n**You may remember our last attempt.**\nThree years ago we asked for $120,000. We reached $47,000, fell short and refunded every pledge in full. This campaign is built differently:\n\n- **A smaller target:** $85,000, not $120,000.\n- **A lease ready to sign:** Once we raise the money, the building's owner will rent us the Majestic for $1 a year for ten years.\n- **A bank behind us:** A local bank has pledged $25,000 if we raise the rest by June 30, 2027.\n- **A head start:** Three local businesses have already pledged $11,000 in writing.\n- **People ready to work:** 46 volunteers have signed up to run the box office and the snack bar.\n\nThat leaves **$49,000** to raise from the community. Last time, our community pledged $47,000. We're asking you to do it again and go a little further.\n\n**Your money is safe either way.**\nThe campaign is all-or-nothing. If we don't reach the full $85,000 by June 30, every pledge will be returned in full, as it was last time. If we do reach it, we'll post a public spending report at the town library every three months, so you can see where every dollar went.\n\n**The audience is here.**\nWhen the Majestic closed, it was still selling about 180 tickets a week. That's an audience that has been waiting for a screen.\n\nThe campaign runs from May 1 to June 30, 2027. Pledge what you can, tell your neighbours, and help us turn the lights back on at the Majestic.\n</final_document>\n\nSome notes on the choices I made:\n\n- **The $49,000 figure is the core of the pitch.** It's the $85,000 total minus the bank's $25,000 and the businesses' $11,000. It's only $2,000 more than the town pledged last time, which makes the goal feel within reach. Please check the sum before it goes out.\n- **The pitch doesn't explain why the first campaign failed,** since you don't know. Instead it lists what has changed.\n- **There are no claims about running costs or long-term sustainability.** You don't have those figures yet, so the only evidence of demand is the 180 tickets a week. Expect backers to ask how the cinema will pay its way. A rough break-even number would make a strong addition before May 1.\n- **Reward tiers, the town name and the bank name** can all go in later without restructuring. The draft is about 300 words, so there's room."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":989,"cache_read_input_tokens":9764,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":989},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5c777ed9-7968-40c0-bdfe-b263cd45fda6","uuid":"1be422e1-83db-405b-be9e-effc6e705e83","timestamp":"2026-11-16T21:21:20.173Z","request_id":"req_011Ch7Jn1FxF7aReFpCDmE6E"}
